      "snippet": "Colombia is importing more liquefied natural gas (LNG) as domestic production continues to fall. A potential drought this fall and winter could limit the availability of hydroelectric generation and boost the country's demand for natural gas power generation. Colombia's government has declared a national disaster in anticipation of a drought resulting from an expected strong El Ni\u00f1o.",
      "source": "U.S. EIA Today in Energy",
      "title": "LNG imports make up increasing share of Colombia's natural gas supply",
      "url": "https://www.eia.gov/todayinenergy/detail.php?id=68364"
