      "snippet": "Global crude oil refinery inputs fell by 4.8 million barrels per day (b/d) in the second quarter of 2026 (2Q26), or 6%, following the start of conflict in late February in the Middle East, according to data from Kpler. Throughput then increased by 1.8 million b/d in the third quarter, primarily as refiners in the region adjusted to new trade flows.",
      "source": "U.S. EIA Today in Energy",
      "title": "Global refinery inputs fell sharply in the second quarter of 2026 before modest recovery",
